"HuidaGene Publishes First-in-Human HG302 Study in Cell, Reporting Molecular Activity and Important Safety Findings in Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy-Press release-HUIDAGENE (https://huidagene.com/new/news/83)\nciteturn663search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: today; SHANGHAI and MIDDLETOWN (DE), OCT 27, 2026— HuidaGene Therapeutics today announced the publication in Cell of results from HG302-01, an investigator-initiated, first-in-human clinical study evaluating HG302, an investigational CRISPR/Cas-based in vivo genome-editing therapy for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD). ... Food and Drug Administration and was evaluated in the HG302-01 first-in-human clinical study.\n\n# HuidaGene Publishes First-in-Human HG302 Study in Cell, Reporting Molecular Activity and Important Safety Findings in Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy\n\n2026.10.27 08:00\n\nPublication provides clinical and preclinical evidence to inform the safety, therapeutic potential, and future development of systemic in-vivo genome editing\n\nSHANGHAI and MIDDLETOWN (DE), OCT 27, 2026— HuidaGene Therapeutics today announced the publication in Cell of results from HG302-01, an investigator-initiated, first-in-human clinical study evaluating HG302, an investigational CRISPR/Cas-based in vivo genome-editing therapy for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD). \n\nThe publication, \"In Vivo Genome-Editing Therapy for Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy: Preclinical Studies and First-in-Human Trial,\" reports preclinical findings and data from four participants treated at two dose levels. The study provides molecular evidence of in vivo genome editing and dystrophin expression in human skeletal muscle, while also documenting a treatment-related fatal serious adverse event and important limitations in predicting and managing severe toxicity associated with systemic AAV delivery.\n\nRead the paper: https://www.cell.com/cell/abstract/S0092-8674(26)01206-7\n\nKey Findings:\n\n• First-in-human clinical evaluation: Four ambulatory boys with DMD received a single intravenous infusion of HG302 at either 5.0×10^{13 }or 1.0×10^{14} vector genomes/kg.\n\n• Molecular evidence of activity: Post-treatment muscle biopsies demonstrated on-target genome editing and detectable dystrophin expression.\n\n• Exploratory functional outcomes: The two participants who completed 12 months of follow-up showed improvements in North Star Ambulatory Assessment (NSAA) scores of 8 and 10 points, respectively, and in 6-minute walk test (6MWT) distance of 106 and 162 meters, respectively.\n\n• Important safety findings: Participant 4, the final participant planned for treatment at that stage, experienced a treatment-related fatal serious adverse event characterized by acute respiratory distress syndrome in the setting of marked complement activation and systemic inflammatory responses. The publication describes the clinical course, safety investigations, and causality assessment.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHuidaGene Therapeutics Provides an Update on the HG302-01 First-in-Human Trial-Press release-HUIDAGENE (https://huidagene.com/new/news/82)\nciteturn663search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; | August 5, 2026 — HuidaGene Therapeutics (“HuidaGene”) today provided an update regarding a fatal serious adverse event in HG302-01, a first-in-human investigator-initiated trial evaluating HG302, an investigational gene-editing therapy for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD). ... HG302 is an investigational CRISPR-based gene-editing therapy designed to restore dystrophin expression in patients with DMD. ... Food and Drug Administration and was evaluated in a first-in-human clinical study.\n\nBack to Latest News\n\n# HuidaGene Therapeutics Provides an Update on the HG302-01 First-in-Human Trial\n\n2026.08.05 22:00\n\nViews:10288\n\nSHANGHAI and MIDDLETOWN, Del. | August 5, 2026 — HuidaGene Therapeutics (“HuidaGene”) today provided an update regarding a fatal serious adverse event in HG302-01, a first-in-human investigator-initiated trial evaluating HG302, an investigational gene-editing therapy for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD).\n\nThis loss saddens us deeply, and we extend our heartfelt condolences to the participant's family. We are grateful for the trust placed in this research by the participant, the family, and all study participants.\n\nIn August 2025, a participant in the high-dose cohort died following administration of HG302. Because serious clinical events require careful verification of the facts and rigorous assessment of causality, HuidaGene conducted a comprehensive clinical and scientific investigation, including laboratory, immunologic, pathological, and post-mortem analyses.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPress release-HUIDAGENE (https://www.huidagene.com/new/news)\nciteturn663search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * Oct 27,2026 HuidaGene Publishes First-in-Human HG302 Study in Cell, Reporting Molecular Activity and Important Safety Findings in Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy Learn More ...   * Apr 09,2025 HuidaGene Announces Broader Adoption of hfCas12Max Through Sublicensing Agreement to Advance Clinical Cell Therapy Programs Learn More\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSCGE Platform (https://scge.mcw.edu/platform/data/report/clinicalTrials/NCT06594094)\nciteturn663search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Eligibility Criteria  | Inclusion Criteria: * Males ≥ 4 and ≤8 years at the time of signing informed consent, with clinical diagnosis of DMD; * DMD gene mutation types are deletions in exons 52, 52-61, or 52-63; * Able to walk at least 10 meters independently; * Willing to cooperate with muscle biopsy test; * Acceptable hematology, clinical chemistry, and urine laboratory parameters. ... Recent Updates  | In August 2025, Patient 4 died following high-dose adminis